4,(PDF) Musical practices and endangered heritage of Atauro island (East Timor) (2022),https://www.academia.edu/86902999/Musical_practices_and_endangered_heritage_of_Atauro_island_East_Timor_2022_,"January 1, 2022 - In the larger landscape of big choruses and gong music, these duets stand as an enigma. They are isolated not only from the surrounding musical practice but also from each other: the language in eastern Timor is Fataluku, a member of the Papuan language family, while in eastern Flores it is Lamaholot, an Austronesian language.",Lamaholot,Austronesian
5,(PDF) (ed.) Austronesian Soundscapes. Performing Arts in Southeast Asia and Oceania,https://www.academia.edu/5322960/_ed_Austronesian_Soundscapes_Performing_Arts_in_Southeast_Asia_and_Oceania,"December 4, 2013 - In the larger landscape of big choruses and gong music, these duets stand as an enigma. They are isolated not only from the surrounding musical practice but also from each other: the language in eastern Timor is Fataluku, a member of the Papuan language family, while in eastern Flores it is Lamaholot, an Austronesian language.",Lamaholot,Austronesian
6,"L’énigme des duos alternés à Flores et Solor (Lamaholot, Indonésie) - HAL-SHS - Sciences de l'Homme et de la Société",https://shs.hal.science/halshs-01411781,"December 7, 2016 - An unusual kind of music was discovered in Flores in the 1930s and was partially described and recorded in the 1990s. This subtle art is still performed nowadays in many villages from Tana ‘Ai to Tanjung Bunga in eastern Flores, some 80 km apart, as well as in the western part of Solor.",Lamaholot,Austronesian
7,Lamaholot Traditional Culture Beyond Easter...,https://larantukaflores.com/lamaholot-culture-beyond-easter/,"May 11, 2026 - Backstrap loom technique. Master weavers in villages around Larantuka produce pieces that international collectors seek. Lamaholot music blends Catholic liturgy with indigenous instruments.",Lamaholot,Austronesian
